=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "B", dense: true)[
  The left ventricle pumps oxygenated blood into the aorta, which carries it to the body.
]

#sol-item(2, "D", dense: true)[
  The pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs.
]

#sol-item(3, "C", dense: true)[
  A short diffusion distance is essential for the exchange of gases, food and waste.
]

#sol-item(4, "A", dense: true)[
  Group O has no antigens on the red cells and both antibodies in the plasma, so it can only receive group O.
]

#sol-item(5, "B", dense: true)[
  The pulmonary and systemic circuits each pass through the heart, so blood passes it twice per circuit.
]

#sol-item(6, "D", dense: true)[
  The left ventricle pumps to the whole body, so it needs the greatest pressure.
]

#sol-item(7, "A", dense: true)[
  Veins carry blood at low pressure, so valves stop it running backwards.
]

#sol-item(8, "C", dense: true)[
  No nucleus leaves more room for haemoglobin, the oxygen-carrying pigment.
]

#sol-item(9, "C", dense: true)[
  Plasma is the straw-coloured fluid that carries the cells and dissolved substances.
]

#sol-item(10, "A", dense: true)[
  White blood cells engulf and digest bacteria, and also produce antibodies.
]

#sol-item(11, "B", dense: true)[
  Deoxygenated blood returns from the body through the vena cava to the right atrium.
]

#sol-item(12, "D", dense: true)[
  Group AB plasma has neither anti-A nor anti-B, so it does not agglutinate transfused cells of any ABO group.
]

#sol-item(13, "A", dense: true)[
  Platelets initiate clotting, converting fibrinogen to fibrin.
]

#sol-item(14, "B", dense: true)[
  It keeps oxygenated and deoxygenated blood apart.
]

#sol-item(15, "C", dense: true)[
  Re-pressurisation after the lungs means the tissues get fully oxygenated blood at full pressure.
]

#sol-item(16, "D", dense: true)[
  The elastic wall stretches with each heartbeat and recoils, smoothing the flow.
]

#sol-item(17, "D", dense: true)[
  Coronary arteries branch from the aorta and supply the cardiac muscle.
]

#sol-item(18, "B", dense: true)[
  It is the only vein that carries food-rich blood to a second organ before returning to the heart.
]

#sol-item(19, "C", dense: true)[
  Lymph is colourless and carries white cells but no red cells.
]

#sol-item(20, "C", dense: true)[
  They close when the ventricles contract, blocking backflow into the atria.
]

#sol-item(21, "B", dense: true)[
  Faster circulation supplies the extra oxygen and glucose that respiring muscle needs.
]

#sol-item(22, "D", dense: true)[
  Chloroplasts are plant organelles; they do not occur in blood.
]

#sol-item(23, "D", dense: true)[
  Arteries carry the pressure wave from each heartbeat, and many lie close to the surface.
]

#sol-item(24, "C", dense: true)[
  The aorta receives blood directly from the left ventricle, so the pressure there is highest.
]

#sol-item(25, "D", dense: true)[
  Red bone marrow is the site of red cell formation in adults.
]

#sol-item(26, "A", dense: true)[
  It is the exception: a vein carrying oxygenated blood towards the heart.
]

#sol-item(27, "C", dense: true)[
  Tissue fluid surrounds the cells and is the medium of exchange between blood and cells.
]

#sol-item(28, "C", dense: true)[
  A faulty valve allows backflow, so the heart must work harder and less blood reaches the tissues.
]

#sol-item(29, "A", dense: true)[
  Cells of similar function in a matrix — the definition of a tissue.
]

#sol-item(30, "D", dense: true)[
  The sounds are made by valves snapping shut, not by the muscle itself.
]

